  "details": "The scaling appears to be double applying to the local first person head bone, so instead of head being a relative scale to neck of .0001 it is an additional 1/9th smaller at 20cm, and 25/9ths larger at 5m.\n\nThis breaks any system that uses scale constraints to return head/muzzle/hair mesh to normal size to make them first person viewable.\n\nIn the example pics the white ruler is scale constrained to head. As the radial is moved away from 1.8m it loses parity with the black reference scale.",
